{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When you acquire a Hebrew slave.</b> A slave who is Hebrew. Or is it rather the slave of a Hebrew — a Canaanite slave whom you purchased from an Israelite — and concerning him does it say 'six years he shall serve'? And how do I fulfill ״וְהִתְנַחַלְתֶּם אֹתָם״ (Leviticus 25) — purchased from a gentile, but one purchased from an Israelite goes free after six? Therefore Scripture says ״כִּי יִמָּכֵר לְךָ אָחִיךָ הָעִבְרִי״ (Deuteronomy 15) — I spoke only of your brother." "<b>When you acquire.</b> From the hand of the court, which sold him for his theft, as it says ״אִם אֵין לוֹ וְנִמְכַּר בִּגְנֵבָתוֹ״. Or is it rather one who sells himself due to his poverty — but one sold by the court does not go free after six? When it says ״וְכִי יָמוּךְ אָחִיךָ עִמָּךְ וְנִמְכַּר לָךְ״ (Leviticus 25), behold, one who sells himself due to his poverty is stated. And what do I fulfill ״כִּי תִקְנֶה״? One sold by the court." "<b>Free.</b> For freedom."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:32.011035712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}